# SRG-APP-000765-AU-000160  -  CAT II
# The Central Log Server must implement a report generation capability that
# supports on-demand audit review and analysis.
#
# Generated from the benchmark and the assessment determinations, then kept
# by hand. Edit this file to change how this requirement is assessed here;
# it is read at run time. Regenerating refreshes the benchmark text in place
# and leaves the criteria, the determination and any verification block as
# they are.

id:              SRG-APP-000765-AU-000160
group:           V-263562
severity:        medium
cat:             CAT II
determination:   APPLICABLE
grade:           C
decidable:       machine
confidence:      derived
cci:             CCI-003825
control_rev5:    AU-7

contribution:    Report generation in Splunk is a saved search object, with its content,
                 its review range and the role permitted to run it all set in application
                 configuration, which is the whole of what the product can contribute to an
                 on-demand review and analysis capability.

governs:         authorize.conf - Used to create roles.
governs:         savedsearches.conf - Saved searches, scheduled reports and alerts.

check:           savedsearches.conf [<stanza name>] search non_empty
check:           savedsearches.conf [<stanza name>] dispatch.earliest_time non_empty
check:           authorize.conf [role_user] search equals enabled
check:           authorize.conf [role_<roleName>] srchIndexesAllowed non_empty
# --- vendor verification: generated, do not edit by hand
corrected:       authorize.conf [role_<roleName>] search equals enabled -> authorize.conf [role_user] search equals enabled
vendor:          authorize.conf [role_<roleName>] search https://help.splunk.com/en/data-management/splunk-enterprise-admin-manual/10.4/configuration-file-reference/10.4.3-configuration-file-reference/authorize.conf
vendor:          savedsearches.conf [<stanza name>] dispatch.earliest_time https://help.splunk.com/en/splunk-enterprise/administer/admin-manual/10.4/configuration-file-reference/10.4.0-configuration-file-reference/savedsearches.conf
vendor:          savedsearches.conf [<stanza name>] dispatch.latest_time https://help.splunk.com/en/splunk-enterprise/administer/admin-manual/10.4/configuration-file-reference/10.4.0-configuration-file-reference/savedsearches.conf
vendor:          savedsearches.conf [<stanza name>] search https://help.splunk.com/en/splunk-enterprise/administer/admin-manual/10.4/configuration-file-reference/10.4.0-configuration-file-reference/savedsearches.conf
# --- end vendor verification

external:        What the report must contain to support review and analysis is an
                 organization-defined parameter recorded in the system security plan.
external:        Whether reviewing personnel are available to run the report on demand, and
                 the review cadence, are organizational procedures.
external:        The closing bound of a report window, which 161 of the 182 saved searches
                 this product ships leave unset because an open end means "to now"; a test
                 for it reports a finding against the product as delivered.

citation:        savedsearches.conf.spec:31 [<stanza name>], :44 search, :564
                 dispatch.earliest_time, :571 dispatch.latest_time;
                 authorize.conf.spec:67-71 [role_<roleName>] <capability> = <enabled>, :292
                 srchIndexesAllowed, :953 [capability::search].
finding:         Assessed at the application layer alone: no saved search implements a
                 report over the audit indexes in scope, or the reviewing role lacks the
                 search capability or search access to those indexes, so the application
                 provides no report generation capability for on-demand review and
                 analysis.
